      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Historical accounts describe Fisher Island's early landscape as a low‑lying tract of coconut palms and mangroves in Biscayne Bay.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fisher_Island%2C_Florida",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Vanderbilt named his glorious retreat on Fisher Island 'Alva Base', also the name of his German‑built 265‑foot diesel yacht.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://fisherislandclub.com/history-page/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fisher Island has no road or causeway; it is reachable only by yacht or private ferry, with guests needing pre‑arranged security clearance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fisher_Island%2C_Florida",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The island emerged after dredging of Government Cut, separating it from the barrier island that became Miami Beach, completed in 1911.",
